      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum for adults: 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWhich of these did you intend?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose**, in which case please confirm the dose and frequency.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional and give me a note to put on the order."
      }
     ],
